course: dictionary
lesson: 3087
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same spelling can mean different things in different places and in different parts of English. Look at the clues around the word to choose the right meaning. «Ee, it's cold!» Here ee is a cry of surprise, like «oh!», because it comes out as a feeling about the cold.
explain: In a story set in Yorkshire, Lancashire or the North East of England, a character might say «Ee, lad». The setting and the word «lad», meaning boy, tell you it is a northern dialect word and not a spelling pattern.
explain: In Scots poems and songs, ee means eye, and its old plural is een. Ask yourself: which meaning fits this sentence? If the poem is about looking or seeing, eye is the likely choice.
explain: Ee is also a letter pair in spelling, making the long "ee" sound, as in «see», «feet», «bee». EE, with capital letters, is the name of a British mobile phone company. Clues in the sentence show you which meaning is meant.
fact: Ee is a dialect cry in Northern England, meaning oh! It is often used as «Ee by gum».
fact: In Scots, ee means eye, and its old plural is een.
fact: As a spelling, the letters ee make one long sound, as in «tree», «sheep» and «green».
fact: EE is the name of a British mobile phone company.
exercise: «Ee, it's freezing out here!» In this sentence, what does ee mean? | *A cry of surprise, like oh! | A Scottish hill | The letters of a long sound in a spelling | A phone company
exercise: In an old Scots poem, ee means what? | Each | Ear | *Eye | Heel
exercise: Which word has the long "ee" sound spelled with the letters ee? | hop | blue | *tree | cat
test: What is EE in everyday life? | A kind of bread | A Scottish hill | *A British mobile phone company | A school subject
test: In old Scots, what is the plural of ee? | eyes | ees | eee | *een
exam: Which meaning of ee fits «Ee, it's cold!»? | Eye | The long ee sound in a spelling | *A cry of surprise, like oh! | A phone company
